+# Delete the disabled CLI YAML translator
+
+Removed `cli/translate/yaml/` (library, test, and BUILD file) and the three stale YAML registration comments in `cli/translate/translate.go`. There was no YAML import in the registry to remove. Its BUILD file already depends only on JS and required no change. Runtime behavior is preserved: `.yaml` was already unregistered.
+
+## Premise verification before editing
+
+- `bazel query '//cli/translate/yaml:all'` returned only `:yaml` and `:yaml_test`.
+- Repository-wide `rg -n 'cli/translate/yaml'` found only the package's own BUILD importpath; no import or external target reference existed. The test embeds `:yaml`, its only declared consumer.
+- The registry contained the commented-out `.yaml: yaml.New()` entry and “Fix and re-enable” comments.
+- `wc -l cli/translate/yaml/*.go` returned 322 implementation lines and 80 test lines (402 total).
+- Attempted `bazel query 'rdeps(//..., //cli/translate/yaml:all, 1)'`. It loaded over 3,400 packages, encountered unrelated Debian snapshot 404s, and eventually waited on unrelated Docker image builds. Stopped that query with SIGTERM (exit 143); it did not produce a usable result. The source/reference verification above independently supports the premise.
+
+## Before / after
+
+Identical commands were used on both states. Counts cover `cli/translate`, not the full CLI binary.
+
+| Measurement | Before | After | Reduction |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Targets (`bazel query '//cli/translate/...'`, line count) | 6 | 4 | 2 |
+| Packages (BUILD files under `cli/translate`) | 4 | 3 | 1 |
+| Go LOC (sum of `splitlines()` for `cli/translate/**/*.go`) | 762 | 357 | 405 |
+| Dependency labels (`bazel query 'deps(//cli/translate/...)'`, unique line count) | 5,952 | 1,404 | 4,548 |
+| External labels (same dependency output, labels starting with `@`) | 5,566 | 1,364 | 4,202 |
+
+The 405 Go-line reduction comprises the deleted 402-line package plus three registry comments. Total diff deletion is 428 lines including BUILD. Dependency counts include source files and implicit dependencies; they do not imply equivalent binary-size or repository-wide dependency reductions. Both dependency queries exited 0.
+
+Reproduce source counts in either state:
+
+```python
+from pathlib import Path
+root = Path('cli/translate')
+print('packages', len(list(root.rglob('BUILD'))))
+print('Go LOC', sum(len(p.read_text().splitlines()) for p in root.rglob('*.go')))
+```
+
+## Validation
+
+Used Bazel 9.3.0rc2, matching `.bazelversion`. Because the `bazel` symlink invokes the BuildBuddy launcher and detached launcher/startup attempts were unreliable, the sustained checks used the same downloaded Bazel binary directly:
+
+`/home/exedev/.cache/bazelisk/downloads/sha256/4e3d5a89541194596abcac40d0547f25c9d673698b709ea96c62c7d0d5379fa2/bin/bazel`
+
+Queries used `--lockfile_mode=off` to avoid changing the shared lockfile. Sustained jobs ran under `nohup`, with logs in `/tmp`, and were polled to completion. To keep the 25 GB VM from running out of disk during the build, reclaimed 4.305 GB of unused Docker builder cache (`docker builder prune -af`) and 1,597,366,882 bytes in 16 large Bazel archive-cache files. Extracted dependencies, build outputs, and source files were retained.
+
+- `bazel --batch query 'rdeps(//cli/..., //cli/translate:translate, 1)' --lockfile_mode=off`: passed; returned `//cli/translate:translate` and `//cli/fix:fix`. Both are covered by the CLI build.
+- `bazel --batch build //cli/... --jobs=2 --remote_executor= --lockfile_mode=off`: passed (exit 0), 142 targets, 11,770 actions, 4,448.616 seconds. Log: `/tmp/yaml-build.log`.
+- `bazel --batch test //cli/translate/... --jobs=2 --remote_executor= --lockfile_mode=off`: passed (exit 0), 1 of 1 test passed (`//cli/translate/js:js_test`), 129.903 seconds. Log: `/tmp/yaml-test.log`.
+- `git diff --check`: passed.
+- `rg -n 'cli/translate/yaml|Fix and re-enable' cli`: no matches after deletion.
+
+## Dependencies and scope
+
+No external module loses its last first-party user. The removed library's sole external dependency, `gopkg.in/yaml.v2`, remains imported by `cli/config/config.go`, `cli/plugin/plugin.go`, and several enterprise packages. Evidence: `rg -n 'gopkg.in/yaml.v2' --glob '*.go'` and `rg -n '@in_gopkg_yaml_v2' cli/config/BUILD cli/plugin/BUILD` (both BUILD files still declare `@in_gopkg_yaml_v2//:yaml_v2`). The removed test's `testify/assert` dependency also remains in `cli/plugin/BUILD` and `cli/translate/js/BUILD`.
+
+No shared dependency files were edited. No replacement tests were added because this removes disabled dead code. No source files outside the allowed scope were changed; `result.md` is the explicitly requested additional deliverable. No push or PR.
